& Delivery","Lead the end-to-end design, development, and deployment of AI-powered capabilities across the DevX Portal and Modular Platform","Translate business needs into scalable AI solutions, ensuring production readiness and measurable impact","Drive innovation in GenAI assistants, agent orchestration, and platform-level automation","AI Architecture & Engineering","Define and guide AI system design decisions, including:","Model selection and evaluation","Prompt engineering strategies","LLM integrations and orchestration frameworks","Data pipelines and knowledge base integration","Establish reusable patterns and extensibility models aligned with enterprise architecture standards","Responsible AI & Governance","Ensure AI initiatives comply with enterprise requirements for:","Security, privacy, and data protection","Regulatory compliance","Ethical AI principles (bias mitigation, explainability, transparency)","Embed governance frameworks and best practices into all AI solutions","Platform Integration & Operations","Integrate AI capabilities into CI/CD pipelines, enabling:","Automated testing and evaluation of AI systems","Continuous monitoring and observability","Performance optimization and reliability","Reduce technical debt and promote maintainable, scalable AI solutions","Cross-Functional Collaboration","Partner with Product Managers, Engineering, Architecture, Security, and Platform teams to:","Identify high-impact AI use cases","Accelerate developer productivity through AI","Drive platform adoption and innovation","Act as a thought leader and advisor on AI-related initiatives","Qualifications","Strong experience with LLMs, GenAI platforms, and prompt engineering","Experience designing scalable AI systems and production-grade ML/AI pipelines","Familiarity with AI governance, compliance, and responsible AI frameworks","Experience integrating AI into developer platforms, DevOps, or CI/CD ecosystems","Strong collaboration and stakeholder management skills","Additional Information","A Serasa Experian é muito mais do que você imagina. Com o propósito de criar um futuro melhor, ampliando oportunidades para pessoas e empresas, no Brasil somos mais de 4 mil pessoas que atuam em diversos times e especialidades. Aqui, cada conhecimento e diversidade se complementa e você pode trabalhar no que mais ama, estamos comprometidos a construir uma cultura inclusiva e um ambiente no qual pessoas possam equilibrar a carreira com seus compromissos e interesses pessoais, prezando pelo bem-estar.","A gente se dedica muito em ser uma das melhores e mais inovadoras empresas para se trabalhar do país, possibilitando experiências e carreiras incríveis para nossas pessoas. Nossa forte abordagem de pessoas em primeiro lugar é reconhecida externamente por meio de diversas certificações de mercado: fomos premiados pelo Great Place To Work™ em 24 países e pela certificação internacional Top Employers, além de sermos reconhecidos como uma das melhores empresas para jovens profissionais e contarmos com uma avaliação de 4,6 no Glassdoor. Cada reconhecimento nos indica que estamos no caminho certo, proporcionando um ambiente de trabalho cada vez melhor para nossos talentos.","Experian Careers - Creating a better tomorrow together","Find out what its like to work for Experian by clicking here"],"skills_raw":["Data and Analytics"],"skills_norm":["Data and Analytics"],"url":"https://www.themuse.com/jobs/experian/ai-specialist-developer-experience-platform-ai","scrape_time":"2026-07-06T14:30:32.393Z"}
{"source_type":"job_platform","source_name":"themuse","page":33,"job_id":"themuse_21776726","job_title":"Senior Solutions Architect (Data & AI)","company_name":"Kyndryl","industry":"Data and Analytics","location":"Barcelona, Spain, Flexible / Remote, Granada, Spain, Madrid, Spain, Seville, Spain","salary_min":"","salary_max":"","experience":"","education":"","publish_date":"2026-06-25","jd_text":"Who We Are \n\nAt Kyndryl, we run and reimagine the mission-critical technology systems that drive advantage for the world's leading businesses. We are at the heart of progress; with proven expertise and a continuous flow of AI-powered insight, enabling smarter decisions, faster innovation, and a lasting competitive edge. For our people-Kyndryls-that means doing purposeful work that powers human progress. Join us and experience a flexible, supportive environment where your well-being is prioritized and your potential can thrive.\n\n The Role \n\nWe are looking for a Senior Solutions Architect to join Kyndryl's Applications, Data & AI (ADAI) practice and lead the end-to-end technology architecture of complex enterprise transformation projects.\n\nThis is a senior, hands-on role for someone who can connect business objectives with scalable, secure, and modern technology solutions. You will be responsible for translating functional and non-functional requirements into clear architectures, guiding delivery teams, and ensuring solutions are technically sound, feasible, operable, and aligned with client outcomes.\n\nYou will work across applications, data, cloud, integration, AI, automation, and operations, helping clients modernize their technology landscape and accelerate business value.\n\n Key Responsibilities \n\nLead end-to-end solution architecture for Applications, Data and AI projects.\n\nTranslate business, functional, and technical requirements into scalable solution designs and delivery roadmaps.\n\nDefine and validate non-functional requirements, including performance, security, resilience, scalability, observability, compliance, and operational readiness.\n\nDesign modern architectures across applications, data platforms, cloud services, APIs, integrations, analytics and AI.\n\nProvide hands-on technical leadership to engineering and delivery teams during implementation.\n\nCreate architecture blueprints, technical designs, integration patterns, migration strategies, and implementation guidance.\n\nParticipate in technical workshops, proof-of-concepts, architecture reviews, and design validation sessions.\n\nIdentify technical risks, dependencies, delivery challenges, and modernization opportunities.\n\nPromote reusable patterns, automation, secure-by-design principles, governance, and engineering excellence.\n\nAct as a trusted advisor to clients and internal teams on architecture and technology decisions.\n\n Who You Are \n\n Required Experience \n\n7+ years of experience as a Solutions Architect, Enterprise Architect, Cloud Architect, Application Architect, Data Architect, Lead Engineer, or similar role.\n\nProven experience designing and delivering enterprise-scale technology solutions.\n\nStrong knowledge of modern application architectures, cloud platforms, data platforms, APIs, integration patterns, and distributed systems.\n\nExperience defining both functional and non-functional requirements for complex technology solutions.\n\nStrong understanding of scalability, resilience, security, observability, performance, compliance, and operational readiness.\n\nPractical experience with cloud-native architectures on Google Cloud, AWS, Azure, or hybrid cloud environments.\n\nExperience with application modernization, migration, integration, data platforms, analytics, AI enablement, or automation initiatives.\n\nStrong communication skills and ability to lead technical discussions, workshops, and architecture reviews.\n\n Preferred Technical Skills \n\nExperience with microservices, APIs, event-driven architectures, containers, Kubernetes, DevSecOps, and CI/CD.\n\nKnowledge of data lakes, data warehouses, lakehouse patterns, streaming, ETL/ELT, governance, and analytics platforms.\n\nFamiliarity with AI and GenAI enablement, MLOps, responsible AI, and enterprise AI adoption patterns.\n\nKnowledge of Infrastructure as Code, DataOps, SRE, observability, automation, and cloud cost optimization.\n\n Being You \n\nThe \"Kyn\" in Kyndryl means kinship, which represents the strong bonds we have with each other, our customers and our communities. We focus on ensuring all Kyndryls feel included and we welcome people of all cultures, backgrounds, and experiences. Even if you don't meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply. We believe in growth, and we're excited to see what you can bring. At Kyndryl, employee feedback has told us that our number one driver of employee engagement is belonging. That sense of belonging - being a valued, respected, trusted member of the team - is fundamental to our culture and fueling great experiences for our customers. This dedication to welcoming everyone into our company means that Kyndryl gives you the ability to thrive and contribute to our culture of empathy and shared success. That's The Kyndryl Way.\n\n What You Can Expect \n\nYour career with us isn't just a job-it's an adventure with purpose. We offer a dynamic, hybrid-friendly culture that supports your well-being and empowers you to grow. Our Be Well programs are thoughtfully designed to support your financial, mental, physical, and social health-because we know that when you feel your best, you do your best. \n\nFrom your very first day, you'll dive into impactful work that powers the systems our customers rely on every day. You won't just contribute-you'll make a difference, tackling meaningful projects that sharpen your skills and fuel your growth.\n\nWe're here to champion your journey. With powerful tools to chart your career path, personalized development goals aligned with your ambitions, and continuous feedback to keep you inspired and on track, you'll have everything you need to thrive and evolve. You'll develop in-demand skills to grow your career and achieve your ambitions with access to cutting-edge learning opportunities-from certifications with Microsoft, Google, and Amazon to coaching and hands-on experiences. And through it all, you'll be part of a culture that values empathy, restless learning, and a devotion to shared success. \n\nWe want you to thrive here-and we're committed to helping you do just that. Ready to make an impact? Join us and help shape what's next.\n\n Get Referred! \n\nIf you know someone that works at Kyndryl, when asked 'How Did You Hear About Us' during the application process, select 'Employee Referral' and enter your contact's Kyndryl email address.","responsibilities":["Who We Are","At Kyndryl, we run and reimagine the mission-critical technology systems that drive advantage for the world's leading businesses. We are at the heart of progress; with proven expertise and a continuous flow of AI-powered insight, enabling smarter decisions, faster innovation, and a lasting competitive edge. For our people-Kyndryls-that means doing purposeful work that powers human progress. Join us and experience a flexible, supportive environment where your well-being is prioritized and your potential can thrive.","The Role","We are looking for a Senior Solutions Architect to join Kyndryl's Applications, Data & AI (ADAI) practice and lead the end-to-end technology architecture of complex enterprise transformation projects.","This is a senior, hands-on role for someone who can connect business objectives with scalable, secure, and modern technology solutions. You will be responsible for translating functional and non-functional requirements into clear architectures, guiding delivery teams, and ensuring solutions are technically sound, feasible, operable, and aligned with client outcomes.","You will work across applications, data, cloud, i