 and technical presentations showcasing Apple's leadership in the AI/ML space.","Contribute to technical resources, training modules, and best practices that scale AI/ML knowledge and capabilities across the global sales organization.","Drive thought leadership internally and externally on the transformative impact of AI/ML on work and learning, with a focus on Apple's contributions and advantages.","Note: This role requires periodic domestic and international travel.","Preferred Qualifications","Experience collaborating with product management, software engineering, and hardware engineering teams to influence platform direction and roadmap priorities.","Hands-on experience with MLX for training, fine-tuning, and running inference with LLMs and other model types on Mac hardware, including awareness of model sizing tradeoffs for on-device deployment.","Demonstrated experience optimizing and deploying machine learning models for on-device inference on Apple Silicon, leveraging Core ML Tools, Metal Performance Shaders, or other optimization techniques.","Practical experience designing or advising on sovereign/private AI cluster deployments using Apple hardware - including Mac selection and configuration, model serving, and remote client access.","Experience building AI/ML capabilities into applications using Model Context Protocol (MCP) - including building MCP servers - and/or App Intents for Siri and Apple Intelligence integration.","Practical experience with generative AI models beyond LLMs (e.g., diffusion models, GANs) and their application in enterprise, education, or government contexts.","Familiarity with Apple developer tooling relevant to AI/ML, including Xcode (including agentic coding features) and the Foundation Models framework.","Hands-on experience with scripting or automation (Swift, Python, Bash, or similar) for testing, deployment, or performance analysis.","Minimum Qualifications","7+ years of experience in a highly technical, customer-facing AI/ML role - such as a Solutions Engineer or Solutions Architect at a major cloud provider; a Field CTO, Technical Evangelist, or Field Engineer at an AI platform or foundation model company; or a Principal Technical Consultant at an enterprise technology organization.","Deep and demonstrable expertise in AI/ML concepts and applications, including:","Machine learning algorithms (supervised, unsupervised, reinforcement learning)","Deep learning architectures (CNNs, RNNs, Transformers, diffusion models)","MLOps principles, data science methodologies, and model deployment strategies","Hands-on experience with major cloud AI/ML platforms (e.g., AWS SageMaker, Azure ML, Google AI Platform)","Deep, hands-on knowledge of Apple's on-device AI/ML stack, including:","Understanding of Apple Silicon architecture and its benefits for on-device inference and other AI/ML workflows","Apple Foundation Models (AFM) and their capabilities and appropriate use cases","Core ML, Core ML Tools, and related on-device inference frameworks","Private Cloud Compute (PCC) architecture and privacy guarantees","Strong ability to articulate the distinction between on-device inference, Private Cloud Compute, and third-party cloud-hosted models - and when each is the right architecture for a given use case.","Demonstrated ability to engage directly with large organizations and partners on strategic AI/ML opportunities, advocating for Apple's platform advantages in real-world use cases.","Pay & Benefits","At Apple, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is determined within a range. This provides the opportunity to progress as you grow and develop within a role. The base pay range for this role is between $207,400 and $311,700, and your base pay will depend on your skills, qualifications, experience, and location.","Apple employees also have the opportunity to become an Apple shareholder through participation in Apple's discretionary employee stock programs. Apple employees are eligible for discretionary restricted stock unit awards, and can purchase Apple stock at a discount if voluntarily participating in Apple's Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You'll also receive benefits including: Comprehensive medical and dental coverage, retirement benefits, a range of discounted products and free services, and for formal education related to advancing your career at Apple, reimbursement for certain educational expenses - including tuition. Additionally, this role might be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments as well as relocation. Learn more about Apple Benefits","Note: Apple benefit, compensation and employee stock programs are subject to eligibility requirements and other terms of the applicable plan or program."],"skills_raw":["Data and Analytics"],"skills_norm":["Data and Analytics"],"url":"https://www.themuse.com/jobs/apple/ww-consulting-engineer-aiml-764f9d","scrape_time":"2026-07-06T14:30:32.393Z"}
{"source_type":"job_platform","source_name":"themuse","page":32,"job_id":"themuse_21757139","job_title":"Securitized Products Group - Quantitative Strategist (ML / LLM) - Tax Oriented Investment Associate","company_name":"JPMorgan Chase","industry":"Data and Analytics","location":"Chicago, IL","salary_min":"","salary_max":"","experience":"","education":"","publish_date":"2026-05-28","jd_text":"Transform how investments get executed by bringing AI-driven automation and analytics directly into the deal lifecycle. Partner side-by-side with senior investment professionals to build tools that accelerate decision-making and improve rigor across complex transactions.\nJob summary\nThe Tax Oriented Investments team is seeking a highly analytical, technically strong Associate to apply machine learning (ML) and large language models (LLMs) to front-office investment workflows. This role sits at the intersection of quantitative research, AI engineering, and deal execution, focused on modernizing deal origination, underwriting, syndication, and asset management through automation, analytics, and AI-enabled decision support.\nJob responsibilities\n \nDevelop a deep understanding of the end-to-end deal lifecycle (origination, underwriting, syndication, asset management) and identify opportunities to improve execution\n \nIdentify process inefficiencies and data gaps across deal workflows; design and implement ML/LLM solutions to improve speed, accuracy, and insight\n \nBuild and deploy LLM-enabled tools to automate review of legal, underwriting, and deal documentation and extract structured insights from unstructured data\n \nEnable high-quality content generation (e.g., investment summaries, credit memos, and investment committee proposals) with appropriate controls and review workflows\n \nDesign and maintain Python-based tools and data pipelines to support market intelligence, deal sourcing insights, and scenario analysis\n \nDeliver portfolio, pipeline, and performance reporting that supports investment decision-making and ongoing asset management\n \nPartner with technology and internal stakeholders on integrations with origination, risk/P&L, and asset management systems; rapidly prototype and iterate based on business feedback\n\nRequired qualifications, capabilities, and skills\n \nBachelor's or advanced degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, Mathematics, or a related quantitative field\n \nDemonstrated expertise in ML and LLMs, with a proven track record of applying them to real-world business problems\n \nStrong programming skills (Python preferred), including building maintainable, production-oriented tools\n \nExperience designing data pipelines and working with structured and unstructured datasets\n \nStrong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills; self-directed with sound independent judgment\n \nExcellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders\n \nGenuine interest in financial markets and motivation to apply technical skills to investment and deal execution problems\n\nPreferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills\n \nPrior experience in deal pitching, origination, underwriting, or investment proposal development\n \nFamiliarity with tax credit investments (e.g., affordable housing, renewable energy) or related structured finance products\n \nExperience integrating analytics/AI solutions into business workflows and enterprise systems\n \nExperience rapidly prototyping solutions and iterating based on stakeholder feedback in a front-office environment\n\n \n\n ABOUT US \n\nJPMorganChase, one of the oldest financial institutions, offers innovative financial solutions to millions of consumers, small businesses and many of the world's most prominent corporate, institutional and government clients under the J.P. Morgan and Chase brands. Our history spans over 200 years and today we are a leader in investment banking, consumer and small business banking, commercial banking, financial transaction processing and asset management.\n\nWe offer a competitive total rewards package including base salary determined based on the role, experience, skill set and location. Those in eligible roles may receive commission-based pay and/or discretionary incentive compensation, paid in the form of cash and/or forfeitable equity, awarded in recognition of individual achievements and contributions. We also offer a range of benefits and programs to meet employee needs, based on eligibility. These benefits include comprehensive health care coverage, on-site health and wellness centers, a retirement savings plan, backup childcare, tuition reimbursement, mental health support, financial coaching and more. Additional details about total compensation and benefits will be provided during the hiring process.\n\nWe recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.\n \nJPMorgan Chase & Co. is an Equal Opportunity Employer, including Disability/Veterans \n\n ABOUT THE TEAM \n\nJ.P. Morgan's Commercial & Investment Bank is a global leader across banking, markets, securities services and payments. Corporations, governments and institutions throughout the world entrust us with their business in more than 100 countries. The Commercial & Investment Bank provides strategic advice, raises capital, manages risk and extends liquidity in markets around the world.","responsibilities":["Transform how investments get executed by bringing AI-driven automation and analytics directly into the deal lifecycle. Partner side-by-side with senior investment professionals to build tools that accelerate decision-making and improve rigor across complex transactions.","Job summary","The Tax Oriented Investments team is seeking a highly analytical, technically strong Associate to apply machine learning (ML) and large language models (LLMs) to front-office investment workflows. This role sits at the intersection of quantitative research, AI engineering, and deal execution, focused on modernizing deal origination, underwriting, syndication, and asset management through automation, analytics, and AI-enabled decision support.","Job responsibilities","Develop a deep understanding of the end-to-end deal lifecycle (origination, underwriting, syndication, asset management) and identify opportunities to improve execution","Identify process inefficiencies and data gaps across deal workflows; design and implement ML/LLM solutions to improve speed, accuracy, and insight","Build and deploy LLM-enabled tools to automate review of legal, underwriting, and deal documentation and extract structured insights from unstructured data","Enable high-quality content generation (e.g., investment summaries, credit memos, and investment committee proposals) with appropriate controls and review workflows","Design and maintain Python-based tools and data pipelines to support market intelligence, deal sourcing insights, and scenario analysis","Deliver portfolio, pipeline, and performance reporting that supports investment decision-making and ongoing asset management","Partner with technology and internal stakeholders on integrations with origination, risk/P&L, and asset management systems; rapidly prototype and iterate based on business feedback","Required qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Bachelor's or advanced degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, Mathematics, or a related quantitative field","Demonstrated expertise in ML and LLMs, with a proven track record of applying them to real-world business problems","Strong programming skills (Python preferred), including building maintainable, production-oriented tools","Experience designing data pipelines and working with structured and unstructured datasets","Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills; self-directed with sound independent judgment","Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders","Genuine interest in financial markets and motivation to apply technical skills to investment and deal execution problems","Preferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Prior experience in deal pitching, origination, underwriting, or investment proposal development","Familiarity with tax credit investments (e.g., affordable housing, renewable energy) or related structured finance products","Experience integrating analytics/AI solutions into business workflows and enterprise systems","Experience rapidly prototyping solutions and iterating based on stakeholder feedback in a front-office environment","ABOUT US","JPMorganChase, one of the oldest financial institutions, offers innovative financial solutions to millions of consumers, small businesses and many of the world's most prominent corporate, institutional and government clients under the J.P. Morgan and Chase brands. Our history spans over 200 years and today we are a leader in investment banking, consumer and small business banking, commercial banking, financial transaction processing and asset management.","We offer a competitive total rewards package including base salary determined based on the role, experience, skill set and location. Those in eligible roles may receive commission-based pay and/or discretionary incentive compensation, paid in the form of cash and/or forfeitable equity, awarded in recognition of individual achievements and contributions. We also offer a range of benefits and programs to meet employee needs, based on eligibility. These benefits include comprehensive health care coverage, on-site health and wellness centers, a retirement savings plan, backup childcare, tuition reimbursement, mental health support, financial coaching and more. Additional details about total compensation and benefits will be provided during the hiring process.","We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.","JPMorgan Chase & Co. is an Equal Opportunity Employer, including Disability/Veterans","ABOUT THE TEAM","J.P. Morgan's Commercial & Investment Bank is a global leader across banking, markets, securities services and payments. Corporations, governments and institutions throughout the world entrust us with their business in more than 100 countries. The Commercial & Investment Bank provides strategic advice, raises capital, manages risk and extends liquidity in markets around the world."],"requirements":["Transform how investments get executed by bringing AI-driven automation and analytics directly into the deal lifecycle. Partner side-by-side with senior investment professionals to build tools that accelerate decision-making and improve rigor across complex transactions.","Job summary","The Tax Oriented Investments team is seeking a highly analytical, technically strong Associate to apply machine learning (ML) and large language models (LLMs) to front-office investment workflows. This role sits at the intersection of quantitative research, AI engineering, and deal execution, focused on modernizing deal origination, underwriting, syndication, and asset management through automation, analytics, and AI-enabled decision support.","Job responsibilities","Develop a deep understanding of the end-to-end deal lifecycle (origination, underwriting, syndication, asset management) and identify opportunities to improve execution","Identify process inefficiencies and data gaps across deal workflows; design and implement ML/LLM solutions to improve speed, accuracy, and insight","Build and deploy LLM-enabled tools to automate review of legal, underwriting, and deal documentation and extract structured insights from unstructured data","Enable high-quality content generation (e.g., investment summaries, credit memos, and investment committee proposals) with appropriate controls and review workflows","Design and maintain Python-based tools and data pipelines to support market intelligence, deal sourcing insights, and scenario analysis","Deliver portfolio, pipeline, and performance reporting that supports investment decision-making and ongoing asset management","Partner with technology and internal stakeholders on integrations with origination, risk/P&L, and asset management systems; rapidly prototype and iterate based on business feedback","Required qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Bachelor's or advanced degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, Mathematics, or a related quantitative field","Demonstrated expertise in ML and LLMs, with a proven track record of applying them to real-world business problems","Strong programming skills (Python preferred), including building maintainable, production-oriented tools","Experience designing data pipelines and working with structured and unstructured datasets","Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills; self-directed with sound independent judgment","Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders","Genuine interest in financial markets and motivation to apply technical skills to investment and deal execution problems","Preferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Prior experience in deal pitching, origination, underwriting, or investment proposal development","Familiarity with tax credit investments (e.g., affordable housing, renewable energy) or related structured finance products","Experience integrating analytics/AI solutions into business workflows and enterprise systems","Experience rapidly prototyping solutions and iterating based on stakeholder feedback in a front-office environment","ABOUT US","JPMorganChase, one of the oldest financial institutions, offers innovative financial solutions to millions of consumers, small businesses and many of the world's most prominent corporate, institutional and government clients under the J.P. Morgan and Chase brands. Our history spans over 200 years and today we are a leader in investment banking, consumer and small business banking, commercial banking, financial transaction processing and asset management.","We offer a competitive total rewards package including base salary determined based on the role, experience, skill set and location. Those in eligible roles may receive commission-based pay and/or discretionary incentive compensation, paid in the form of cash and/or forfeitable equity, awarded in recognition of individual achievements and contributions. We also offer a range of benefits and programs to meet employee needs, based on eligibility. These benefits include comprehensive health care coverage, on-site health and wellness centers, a retirement savings plan, backup childcare, tuition reimbursement, mental health support, financial coaching and more. Additional details about total compensation and benefits will be provided during the hiring process.","We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.","JPMorgan Chase & Co. is an Equal Opportunity Employer, including Disability/Veterans","ABOUT THE TEAM","J.P. Morgan's Commercial & Investment Bank is a global leader across banking, markets, securities services and payments. Corporations, governments and institutions throughout the world entrust us with their business in more than 100 countries. The Commercial & Investment Bank provides strategic advice, raises capital, manages risk and extends liquidity in markets around the world."],"skills_raw":["Data and Analytics"],"skills_norm":["Data and Analytics"],"url":"https://www.themuse.com/jobs/jpmorganchase/securitized-products-group-quantitative-strategist-ml-llm-tax-oriented-investment-associate","scrape_time":"2026-07-06T14:30:32.393Z"}
{"source_type":"job_platform","source_name":"themuse","page":39,"job_id":"themuse_21918370","job_title":"WW Consulting Engineer - AI/ML","company_name":"Apple","industry":"Data and Analytics","location":"Chicago, IL","salary_min":"","salary_max":"","experience":"","education":"","publish_date":"2026-07-05","jd_text":"Imagine what you could do here. The people here at Apple don't just create products - they create the kind of wonder that's revolutionized entire industries. It's the diversity of those people and their ideas that inspires the innovation that runs through everything we do, from amazing technology to industry-leading environmental efforts. Join Apple, and help us leave the world better than we found it.\n\nApple's Sales organization generates the revenue needed to fuel our ongoing development of products and services. This in turn enriches the lives of hundreds of millions of people around the world. Our sales team is in many ways the face of Apple to our largest customers. Our Business and Education customers around the globe need to know that Apple is committed to their success and that our technologies will seamlessly integrate into their environments.\n\nAs a Worldwide Consulting Engineer focused on AI/ML within Apple's Enterprise, Education & Government sales organization, you will be a critical part of a global team responsible for ensuring the technical integrity and strategic positioning of Apple platforms and solutions in the rapidly evolving AI/ML landscape. You will be a strategic advisor, technical visionary, and subject matter expert, shaping the future of Apple's presence in business and education organizations worldwide.\n\nYou will provide deep domain expertise across cloud, hybrid, and on-device/edge AI/ML solutions, demonstrating Apple's unique advantages in end-user compute and mobility - including Apple Silicon, the Neural Engine, Apple Foundation Models, and Private Cloud Compute - and how they extend to critical areas such as industry trends, use case development, and the transformative impact of AI/ML on work and learning.\n\nYou will be instrumental in identifying and surfacing technical barriers to broader adoption of Apple technologies within Business and Education environments, effectively communicating customer needs and insights directly to Software, Hardware, Services, and Product teams. You will be a key bridge between customers and Apple's engineering teams, ensuring that market trends are reflected in Apple's product roadmap.\n\n Description \n\nIn this role, you will:\n\nEmpower and educate global Field Sales Engineers, customers, and partners on Apple's product advantages - Mac, iOS, iPadOS, Apple Silicon - across cloud-based, hybrid, on-device, and edge AI/ML architectures, with fluency in where each deployment model is most appropriate.\n\nDevelop and articulate compelling technical value propositions for Apple platforms across enterprise, education, and government sectors, with particular depth around Apple Foundation Models (AFM), on-device inference, and Apple Intelligence features.\n\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams - including Product Marketing, Business Markets, Engineering, and Sales Leadership - to define and refine go-to-market strategies and AI/ML solution offerings leveraging Apple technology.\n\nEngage directly with strategic customers and partners in deep technical discussions, understanding their AI/ML initiatives and positioning Apple's unique capabilities - including Private Cloud Compute (PCC) privacy guarantees - to meet their needs and drive innovation.\n\nAdvise on scalability strategies for on-device and edge AI/ML solutions, determining when a single node is sufficient versus when a cluster approach is necessary, including hardware selection and model serving architecture for sovereign AI deployments.\n\nGuide enterprise customers and developers on integrating AI/ML capabilities into applications using approaches such as Model Context Protocol (MCP) and App Intents, and how to evaluate tradeoffs between them.\n\nMonitor and analyze emerging AI/ML trends, technologies, and industry shifts - translating insights into actionable guidance for field teams and leadership, with a continuous learning mindset.\n\nLead key customer and partner engagements including executive briefings, workshops, proof-of-concepts, and technical presentations showcasing Apple's leadership in the AI/ML space.\n\nContribute to technical resources, training modules, and best practices that scale AI/ML knowledge and capabilities across the global sales organization.\n\nDrive thought leadership internally and externally on the transformative impact of AI/ML on work and learning, with a focus on Apple's contributions and advantages.\n\nNote: This role requires periodic domestic and international travel.\n\n Preferred Qualifications \n\nExperience collaborating with product management, software engineering, and hardware engineering teams to influence platform direction and roadmap priorities.\n\nHands-on experience with MLX for training, fine-tuning, and running inference with LLMs and other model types on Mac hardware, including awareness of model sizing tradeoffs for on-device deployment.\n\nDemonstrated experience optimizing and deploying machine learning models for on-device inference on Apple Silicon, leveraging Core ML Tools, Metal Performance Shaders, or other optimization techniques.\n\nPractical experience designing or advising on sovereign/private AI cluster deployments using Apple hardware - including Mac selection and configuration, model serving, and remote client access.\n\nExperience building AI/ML capabilities into applications using Model Context Protocol (MCP) - including building MCP servers - and/or App Intents for Siri and Apple Intelligence integration.\n\nPractical experience with generative AI models beyond LLMs (e.g., diffusion models, GANs) and their application in enterprise, education, or government contexts.\n\nFamiliarity with Apple developer tooling relevant to AI/ML, including Xcode (including agentic coding features) and the Foundation Models framework.\n\nHands-on experience with scripting or automation (Swift, Python, Bash, or similar) for testing, deployment, or performance analysis.\n\n Minimum Qualifications \n\n7+ years of experience in a highly technical, customer-facing AI/ML role - such as a Solutions Engineer or Solutions Architect at a major cloud provider; a Field CTO, Technical Evangelist, or Field Engineer at an AI platform or foundation model company; or a Principal Technical Consultant at an enterprise technology organization.\n\nDeep and demonstrable expertise in AI/ML concepts and applications, including:\n\nMachine learning algorithms (supervised, unsupervised, reinforcement learning)\n\nDeep learning architectures (CNNs, RNNs, Transformers, diffusion models)\n\nMLOps principles, data science methodologies, and model deployment strategies\n\nHands-on experience with major cloud AI/ML platforms (e.g., AWS SageMaker, Azure ML, Google AI Platform)\n\nDeep, hands-on knowledge of Apple's on-device AI/ML stack, including:\n\nUnderstanding of Apple Silicon architecture and its benefits for on-device inference and other AI/ML workflows\n\nApple Foundation Models (AFM) and their capabilities and appropriate use cases\n\nCore ML, Core ML Tools, and related on-device inference frameworks\n\nPrivate Cloud Compute (PCC) architecture and privacy guarantees\n\nStrong ability to articulate the distinction between on-device inference, Private Cloud Compute, and third-party cloud-hosted models - and when each is the right architecture for a given use case.\n\nDemonstrated ability to engage directly with large organizations and partners on strategic AI/ML opportunities, advocating for Apple's platform advantages in real-world use cases.\n\n Pay & Benefits \n\nAt Apple, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is determined within a range. This provides the opportunity to progress as you grow and develop within a role. The base pay range for this role is between $207,400 and $311,700, and your base pay will depend on your skills, qualifications, experience, and location.\n\nApple employees also have the opportunity to become an Apple shareholder through participation in Apple's discretionary employee stock programs. Apple employees are eligible for discretionary restricted stock unit awards, and can purchase Apple stock at a discount if voluntarily participating in Apple's Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You'll also receive benefits including: Comprehensive medical and dental coverage, retirement benefits, a range of discounted products and free services, and for formal education related to advancing your career at Apple, reimbursement for certain educational expenses - including tuition. Additionally, this role might be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments as well as relocation. Learn more about Apple Benefits\n\nNote: Apple benefit, compensation and employee stock programs are subject to eligibility requirements and other terms of the applicable plan or program.","responsibilities":["Imagine what you could do here. The people here at Apple don't just create products - they create the kind of wonder that's revolutionized entire industries. It's the diversity of those people and their ideas that inspires the innovation that runs through everything we do, from amazing technology to industry-leading environmental efforts. Join Apple, and help us leave the world better than we found it.","Apple's Sales organization generates the revenue needed to fuel our ongoing development of products and services. This in turn enriches the lives of hundreds of millions of people around the world. Our sales team is in many ways the face of Apple to our largest customers. Our Business and Education customers around the globe need to know that Apple is committed to their success and that our technologies will seamlessly integrate into their environments.","As a Worldwide Consulting Engineer focused on AI/ML within Apple's Enterprise, Education & Government sales organization, you will be a critical part of a global team responsible for ensuring the technical integrity and strategic positioning of Apple platforms and solutions in the rapidly evolving AI/ML landscape. You will be a strategic advisor, technical visionary, and subject matter expert, shaping the future of Apple's presence in business and education organizations worldwide.","You will provide deep domain expertise across cloud, hybrid, and on-device/edge AI/ML solutions, demonstrating Apple's unique advantages in end-user compute and mobility - including Apple Silicon, the Neural Engine, Apple Foundation Models, and Private Cloud Compute - and how they extend to critical areas such as industry trends, use case development, and the transformative impact of AI/ML on work and learning.","You will be instrumental in identifying and surfacing technical barriers to broader adoption of Apple technologies within Business and Education environments, effectively communicating customer needs and insights directly to Software, Hardware, Services, and Product teams. You will be a key bridge between customers and Apple's engineering teams, ensuring that market trends are reflected in Apple's product roadmap.","Description","In this role, you will:","Empower and educate global Field Sales Engineers, customers, and partners on Apple's product advantages - Mac, iOS, iPadOS, Apple Silicon - across cloud-based, hybrid, on-device, and edge AI/ML architectures, with fluency in where each deployment model is most appropriate.","Develop and articulate compelling technical value propositions for Apple platforms across enterprise, education, and government sectors, with particular depth around Apple Foundation Models (AFM), on-device inference, and Apple Intelligence features.","Collaborate with cross-functional teams - including Product Marketing, Business Markets, Engineering, and Sales Leadership - to define and refine go-to-market strategies and AI/ML solution offerings leveraging Apple technology.","Engage directly with strategic customers and partners in deep technical discussions, understanding their AI/ML initiatives and positioning Apple's unique capabilities - including Private Cloud Compute (PCC) privacy guarantees - to meet their needs and drive innovation.","Advise on scalability strategies for on-device and edge AI/ML solutions, determining when a single node is sufficient versus when a cluster approach is necessary, including hardware selection and model serving architecture for sovereign AI deployments.","Guide enterprise customers and developers on integrating AI/ML capabilities into applications using approaches such as Model Context Protocol (MCP) and App Intents, and how to evaluate tradeoffs between them.","Monitor and analyze emerging AI/ML trends, technologies, and industry shifts - translating insights into actionable guidance for field teams and leadership, with a continuous learning mindset.","Lead key customer and partner engagements including executive briefings, workshops, proof-of-concepts, and technical presentations showcasing Apple's leadership in the AI/ML space.","Contribute to technical resources, training modules, and best practices that scale AI/ML knowledge and capabilities across the global sales organization.","Drive thought leadership internally and externally on the transformative impact of AI/ML on work and learning, with a focus on Apple's contributions and advantages.","Note: This role requires periodic domestic and international travel.","Preferred Qualifications","Experience collaborating with product management, software engineering, and hardware engineering teams to influence platform direction and roadmap priorities.","Hands-on experience with MLX for training, fine-tuning, and running inference with LLMs and other model types on Mac hardware, including awareness of model sizing tradeoffs for on-device deployment.","Demonstrated experience optimizing and deploying machine learning models for on-device inference on Apple Silicon, leveraging Core ML Tools, Metal Performance Shaders, or other optimization techniques.","Practical experience designing or advising on sovereign/private AI cluster deployments using Apple hardware - including Mac selection and configuration, model serving, and remote client access.","Experience building AI/ML capabilities into applications using Model Context Protocol (MCP) - including building MCP servers - and/or App Intents for Siri and Apple Intelligence integration.","Practical experience with generative AI models beyond LLMs (e.g., diffusion models, GANs) and their application in enterprise, education, or government contexts.","Familiarity with Apple developer tooling relevant to AI/ML, including Xcode (including agentic coding features) and the Foundation Models framework.","Hands-on experience with scripting or automation (Swift, Python, Bash, or similar) for testing, deployment, or performance analysis.","Minimum Qualifications","7+ years of experience in a highly technical, customer-facing AI/ML role - such as a Solutions Engineer or Solutions Architect at a major cloud provider; a Field CTO, Technical Evangelist, or Field Engineer at an AI platform or foundation model company; or a Principal Technical Consultant at an enterprise technology organization.","Deep and demonstrable expertise in AI/ML concepts and applications, including:","Machine learning algorithms (supervised, unsupervised, reinforcement learning)","Deep learning architectures (CNNs, RNNs, Transformers, diffusion models)","MLOps principles, data science methodologies, and model deployment strategies","Hands-on experience with major cloud AI/ML platforms (e.g., AWS SageMaker, Azure ML, Google AI Platform)","Deep, hands-on knowledge of Apple's on-device AI/ML stack, including:","Understanding of Apple Silicon architecture and its benefits for on-device inference and other AI/ML workflows","Apple Foundation Models (AFM) and their capabilities and appropriate use cases","Core ML, Core ML Tools, and related on-device inference frameworks","Private Cloud Compute (PCC) architecture and privacy guarantees","Strong ability to articulate the distinction between on-device inference, Private Cloud Compute, and third-party cloud-hosted models - and when each is the right architecture for a given use case.","Demonstrated ability to engage directly with large organizations and partners on strategic AI/ML opportunities, advocating for Apple's platform advantages in real-world use cases.","Pay & Benefits","At Apple, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is determined within a range. This provides the opportunity to progress as you grow and develop within a role. The base pay range for this role is between $207,400 and $311,700, and your base pay will depend on your skills, qualifications, experience, and location.","Apple employees also have the opportunity to become an Apple shareholder through participation in Apple's discretionary employee stock programs. Apple employees are eligible for discretionary restricted stock unit awards, and can purchase Apple stock at a discount if voluntarily participating in Apple's Employee Stock Purchase Plan. You'll also receive benefits including: Comprehensive medical and dental coverage, retirement benefits, a range of discounted products and free services, and for formal education related to advancing your career at Apple, reimbursement for certain educational expenses - including tuition. Additionally, this role might be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments as well as relocation. Learn more about Apple Benefits","Note: Apple benefit, compensation and employee stock programs are subject to eligibility requirements and other terms of the applicable plan or program."],"requirements":["Imagine what you could do here. The people here at Apple don't just create products - they create the kind of wonder that's revolutionized entire industries. It's the diversity of those people and their ideas that inspires the innovation that runs through everything we do, from amazing technology to industry-leading environmental efforts. Join Apple, and help us leave the world better than we found it.","Apple's Sales organization generates the revenue needed to fuel our ongoing development of products and services. This in turn enriches the lives of hundreds of millions of people around the world. Our sales team is in many ways the face of Apple to our largest customers. Our Business and Education customers around the globe need to know that Apple is committed to their success and that our technologies will seamlessly integrate into their environments.","As a Worldwide Consulting Engineer focused on AI/ML within Apple's Enterprise, Education & Government sales organization, you will be a critical part of a global team responsible for ensuring the technical integrity and strategic positioning of Apple platforms and solutions in the rapidly evolving AI/ML landscape. You will be a strategic advisor, technical visionary, and subject matter expert, shaping the future of Apple's presence in business and education organizations worldwide.","You will provide deep domain expertise across cloud, hybrid, and on-device/edge AI/ML solutions, demonstrating Apple's unique advantages in end-user compute and mobility - including Apple Silicon, the Neural Engine, Apple Foundation Models, and Private Cloud Compute - and how they extend to critical areas such as industry trends, use case development, and the transformative impact of AI/ML on work and learning.","You will be instrumental in identifying and surfacing technical barriers to broader adoption of Apple technologies within Business and Education environments, effectively communicating customer needs and insights directly to Software, Hardware, Services,