employment screening may include employment history, education and other information (such as media information) that may be necessary for determining your qualifications and suitability for the position."],"skills_raw":["Data and Analytics"],"skills_norm":["Data and Analytics"],"url":"https://www.themuse.com/jobs/bookingcom/machine-learning-scientist-ii-travel-llms-modelling","scrape_time":"2026-07-06T14:30:32.393Z"}
{"source_type":"job_platform","source_name":"themuse","page":39,"job_id":"themuse_21505302","job_title":"Lead AI/ML Engineer","company_name":"JPMorgan Chase","industry":"Data and Analytics","location":"Dublin, Ireland","salary_min":"","salary_max":"","experience":"","education":"","publish_date":"2026-06-18","jd_text":"Join us to shape the future of AI at JPMorganChase. You will lead transformative projects that empower teams and drive business value. As an AI/ML Vice President, you'll unlock career growth, expand your technical skills, and make a meaningful impact. Experience a collaborative culture where your ideas matter and your expertise is valued. Discover the benefits of working with industry leaders and advancing enterprise innovation.\n\nAs an AI/ML Vice President in our AI Engineering team, you will design and deliver enterprise-scale AI/ML solutions that drive business outcomes. You will work closely with us to set engineering standards, mentor talented teams, and ensure our solutions are secure, scalable, and production ready. You will help shape our team culture, foster innovation, and contribute to the broader AI strategy. Your leadership will inspire us to push boundaries and create lasting impact.\n\nJob responsibilities\n\n \nLead the end-to-end design and implementation of AI/ML systems, from concept through production.\n \nRemain hands-on in code, setting high standards for engineering quality and reliability.\n \nDefine architectural patterns for LLM-based systems, agent workflows, and AI-enabled services.\n \nEstablish AI roadmaps, investment priorities, and reference architectures.\n \nMake build/buy decisions and set patterns for model lifecycle, data contracts, and platform services.\n \nGuide teams in building Copilot-integrated solutions that enhance enterprise productivity.\n \nDefine KPIs/OKRs and articulate ROI for AI initiatives; report status and risks to executives.\n \nManage vendors and ensure external solutions are approved before implementation.\n \nDrive delivery of production-grade AI solutions with strong observability and operational rigor.\n \nEstablish best practices for prompt engineering, agent design, evaluation, and monitoring.\n \nEnsure AI/ML solutions integrate cleanly with existing platforms, APIs, and enterprise systems.\n\nRequired qualifications, capabilities, and skills\n\n \nAdvanced degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or equivalent experience.\n \nMinimum 6 years of hands-on programming experience delivering complex systems to production.\n \nDeep expertise in Python and modern software engineering practices.\n \nExpertise in scalable systems, including microservices, service meshes, and distributed data processing.\n \nProven experience with LLMs/GenAI patterns such as fine-tuning, retrieval-augmented generation, evaluation, and safety.\n \nStrong communication skills across technical and executive audiences.\n\nPreferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills\n\n \nExperience leading or scaling Microsoft 365 Copilot or Copilot Agent-based solutions.\n \nFamiliarity with Azure, Microsoft Graph, or enterprise productivity platforms.\n \nTrack record of balancing hands-on engineering leadership with strategic influence.\n \nSystems thinking; balances speed, safety, and value creation.\n \nOperational excellence in risk management, resiliency, and continuous improvement.\n\n \n\n ABOUT US \n\nJ.P. Morgan is a global leader in financial services, providing strategic advice and products to the world's most prominent corporations, governments, wealthy individuals and institutional investors. Our first-class business in a first-class way approach to serving clients drives everything we do. We strive to build trusted, long-term partnerships to help our clients achieve their business objectives.\n\nWe recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation. \n\n ABOUT THE TEAM \n\nOur professionals in our Corporate Functions cover a diverse range of areas from finance and risk to human resources and marketing. Our corporate teams are an essential part of our company, ensuring that we're setting our businesses, clients, customers and employees up for success.","responsibilities":["Join us to shape the future of AI at JPMorganChase. You will lead transformative projects that empower teams and drive business value. As an AI/ML Vice President, you'll unlock career growth, expand your technical skills, and make a meaningful impact. Experience a collaborative culture where your ideas matter and your expertise is valued. Discover the benefits of working with industry leaders and advancing enterprise innovation.","As an AI/ML Vice President in our AI Engineering team, you will design and deliver enterprise-scale AI/ML solutions that drive business outcomes. You will work closely with us to set engineering standards, mentor talented teams, and ensure our solutions are secure, scalable, and production ready. You will help shape our team culture, foster innovation, and contribute to the broader AI strategy. Your leadership will inspire us to push boundaries and create lasting impact.","Job responsibilities","Lead the end-to-end design and implementation of AI/ML systems, from concept through production.","Remain hands-on in code, setting high standards for engineering quality and reliability.","Define architectural patterns for LLM-based systems, agent workflows, and AI-enabled services.","Establish AI roadmaps, investment priorities, and reference architectures.","Make build/buy decisions and set patterns for model lifecycle, data contracts, and platform services.","Guide teams in building Copilot-integrated solutions that enhance enterprise productivity.","Define KPIs/OKRs and articulate ROI for AI initiatives; report status and risks to executives.","Manage vendors and ensure external solutions are approved before implementation.","Drive delivery of production-grade AI solutions with strong observability and operational rigor.","Establish best practices for prompt engineering, agent design, evaluation, and monitoring.","Ensure AI/ML solutions integrate cleanly with existing platforms, APIs, and enterprise systems.","Required qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Advanced degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or equivalent experience.","Minimum 6 years of hands-on programming experience delivering complex systems to production.","Deep expertise in Python and modern software engineering practices.","Expertise in scalable systems, including microservices, service meshes, and distributed data processing.","Proven experience with LLMs/GenAI patterns such as fine-tuning, retrieval-augmented generation, evaluation, and safety.","Strong communication skills across technical and executive audiences.","Preferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Experience leading or scaling Microsoft 365 Copilot or Copilot Agent-based solutions.","Familiarity with Azure, Microsoft Graph, or enterprise productivity platforms.","Track record of balancing hands-on engineering leadership with strategic influence.","Systems thinking; balances speed, safety, and value creation.","Operational excellence in risk management, resiliency, and continuous improvement.","ABOUT US","J.P. Morgan is a global leader in financial services, providing strategic advice and products to the world's most prominent corporations, governments, wealthy individuals and institutional investors. Our first-class business in a first-class way approach to serving clients drives everything we do. We strive to build trusted, long-term partnerships to help our clients achieve their business objectives.","We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.","ABOUT THE TEAM","Our professionals in our Corporate Functions cover a diverse range of areas from finance and risk to human resources and marketing. Our corporate teams are an essential part of our company, ensuring that we're setting our businesses, clients, customers and employees up for success."],"requirements":["Join us to shape the future of AI at JPMorganChase. You will lead transformative projects that empower teams and drive business value. As an AI/ML Vice President, you'll unlock career growth, expand your technical skills, and make a meaningful impact. Experience a collaborative culture where your ideas matter and your expertise is valued. Discover the benefits of working with industry leaders and advancing enterprise innovation.","As an AI/ML Vice President in our AI Engineering team, you will design and deliver enterprise-scale AI/ML solutions that drive business outcomes. You will work closely with us to set engineering standards, mentor talented teams, and ensure our solutions are secure, scalable, and production ready. You will help shape our team culture, foster innovation, and contribute to the broader AI strategy. Your leadership will inspire us to push boundaries and create lasting impact.","Job responsibilities","Lead the end-to-end design and implementation of AI/ML systems, from concept through production.","Remain hands-on in code, setting high standards for engineering quality and reliability.","Define architectural patterns for LLM-based systems, agent workflows, and AI-enabled services.","Establish AI roadmaps, investment priorities, and reference architectures.","Make build/buy decisions and set patterns for model lifecycle, data contracts, and platform services.","Guide teams in building Copilot-integrated solutions that enhance enterprise productivity.","Define KPIs/OKRs and articulate ROI for AI initiatives; report status and risks to executives.","Manage vendors and ensure external solutions are approved before implementation.","Drive delivery of production-grade AI solutions with strong observability and operational rigor.","Establish best practices for prompt engineering, agent design, evaluation, and monitoring.","Ensure AI/ML solutions integrate cleanly with existing platforms, APIs, and enterprise systems.","Required qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Advanced degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or equivalent experience.","Minimum 6 years of hands-on programming experience delivering complex systems to production.","Deep expertise in Python and modern software engineering practices.","Expertise in scalable systems, including microservices, service meshes, and distributed data processing.","Proven experience with LLMs/GenAI patterns such as fine-tuning, retrieval-augmented generation, evaluation, and safety.","Strong communication skills across technical and executive audiences.","Preferred qualifications, capabilities, and skills","Experience leading or scaling Microsoft 365 Copilot or Copilot Agent-based solutions.","Familiarity with Azure, Microsoft Graph, or enterprise productivity platforms.","Track record of balancing hands-on engineering leadership with strategic influence.","Systems thinking; balances speed, safety, and value creation.","Operational excellence in risk management, resiliency, and continuous improvement.","ABOUT US","J.P. Morgan is a global leader in financial services, providing strategic advice and products to the world's most prominent corporations, governments, wealthy individuals and institutional investors. Our first-class business in a first-class way approach to serving clients drives everything we do. We strive to build trusted, long-term partnerships to help our clients achieve their business objectives.","We recognize that our people are our strength and the diverse talents they bring to our global workforce are directly linked to our success. We are an equal opportunity employer and place a high value on diversity and inclusion at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital or veteran status, pregnancy or disability, or any other basis protected under applicable law. We also make reasonable accommodations for applicants' and employees' religious practices and beliefs, as well as mental health or physical disability needs. Visit our FAQs for more information about requesting an accommodation.","ABOUT THE TEAM","Our professionals in our Corporate Functions cover a diverse range of areas from finance and risk to human resources and marketing. Our corporate teams are an essential part of our company, ensuring that we're setting our businesses, clients, customers and employees up for success."],"skills_raw":["Data and Analytics"],"skills_norm":["Data and Analytics"],"url":"https://www.themuse.com/jobs/jpmorganchase/lead-aiml-engineer-e28c78","scrape_time":"2026-07-06T14:30:32.393Z"}
{"source_type":"job_platform","source_name":"themuse","page":1,"job_id":"themuse_17973175","job_title":"LLM Agents Platform R&D intern -AI Innovation Center-2025 Start","company_name":"TikTok","industry":"Data and Analytics","location":"Singapore","salary_min":"","salary_max":"","experience":"","education":"","publish_date":"2025-02-21","jd_text":"Responsibilities \n\n TikTok is the leading destination for short-form mobile video. At TikTok, our mission is to inspire creativity and bring joy. TikTok's global headquarters are in Los Angeles and Singapore, and its offices include New York, London, Dublin, Paris, Berlin, Dubai, Jakarta, Seoul, and Tokyo. \n\nWhy Join Us\nCreation is the core of TikTok's purpose. Our platform is built to help imagination thrive. This is doubly true of the teams that make TikTok possible.\nTogether, we inspire creativity and bring joy - a mission we all believe in and aim towards achieving every day.\nTo us, every challenge, no matter how difficult, is an opportunity; to learn, to innovate, and to grow as one team. Status quo? Never. Courage? Always.\nAt TikTok, we create together and grow together. That's how we drive impact - for ourselves, our company, and the communities we serve.\nJoin us.\n\nAbout The Team:\nThe mission of the TikTok Eng-AI Innovation Center is to explore cutting-edge AGI technologies, including but not limited to LLM, multi-modal LLM (video/image/audio/text/code), etc., to let machine better understand user creations on Tiktok platform. Regarding to video/image/audio/text, enhanced content understanding can bring better user experience of searching, recommendation, and can more accurately identify and defend internet abuse and fraud on our platform. Regarding to code, our developed LLM aims to automatically re-organize/optimize Tiktok codebase, and make the code/coding become more accessible for Tiktok engineers. \n\nWe are looking for talented individuals to join us for an internship in 2025. PhD Internships at TikTok aim to provide students with the opportunity to actively contribute to our products and research, and to the organization's future plans and emerging technologies.\n\nCandidates can apply to a maximum of two positions and will be considered for jobs in the order you apply. The application limit is applicable to TikTok and its affiliates' jobs globally. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis - we encourage you to apply early.\n\nSuccessful candidates must be able to commit to at least 3 months long internship period.\n\nThe main job directions include:\n1. Research on LLM Agent methodology, how to build better performance/low cost/stability agents;\n2. Explore cutting-edge technologies related to LLM Agent engineering platform(AgentOps), covering areas such as RAG, Reasoning, Planning, Toolkits, Multi-Agents Coordination.\n3. Construct a high-performance, cost-effective large-model agent service architecture that ensures high service availability.;\n4. Explore the application of frontier LLM agents, like multi-modal video agents, multi-agents coordination on Code AI, etc.\n\n Qualifications \n\n Minimum Qualifications\n1. PhD with Computer Science or related fields, with good communication and teamwork skills;\n2. Excellent coding ability, data structures, and fundamental algorithm skills, proficient in C/C++ or Python, winners of competitions such as ACM/ICPC, NOI/IOI, Top Coder, Kaggle, etc. are preferred\n3. In-depth research and collaboration with researchers from top-tier universities worldwide;\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n1. Passion for technology, good communication skills and team spirit\n\nTikTok is committed to creating an inclusive space where employees are valued for their skills, experiences, and unique perspectives. Our platform connects people from across the globe and so does our workplace. At TikTok, our mission is to inspire creativity and bring joy. To achieve that goal, we are committed to celebrating our diverse voices and to creating an environment that reflects the many communities we reach. We are passionate about this and hope you are too.\n\nFor TikTok\nBy submitting an application for this role, you accept and agree to our global applicant privacy policy, which may be accessed here: https://careers.tiktok.com/legal/privacy.\n\nFor TikTok\nIf you have any questions, please reach out to us at apac-earlycareers@tiktok.com","responsibilities":["Responsibilities","TikTok is the leading destination for short-form mobile video. At TikTok, our mission is to inspire creativity and bring joy. TikTok's global headquarters are in Los Angeles and Singapore, and its offices include New York, London, Dublin, Paris, Berlin, Dubai, Jakarta, Seoul, and Tokyo.","Why Join Us","Creation is the core of TikTok's purpose. Our platform is built to help imagination thrive. This is doubly true of the teams that make TikTok possible.","Together, we inspire creativity and bring joy - a mission we all believe in and aim towards achieving every day.","To us, every challenge, no matter how difficult, is an opportunity; to learn, to innovate, and to grow as one team. Status quo? Never. Courage? Always.","At TikTok, we create together and grow together. That's how we drive impact - for ourselves, our company, and the communities we serve.","Join us.","About The Team:","The mission of the TikTok Eng-AI Innovation Center is to explore cutting-edge AGI technologies, including but not limited to LLM, multi-modal LLM (video/image/audio/text/code), etc., to let machine better understand user creations on Tiktok platform. Regarding to video/image/audio/text, enhanced content understanding can bring better user experience of searching, recommendation, and can more accurately identify and defend internet abuse and fraud on our platform. Regarding to code, our developed LLM aims to automatically re-organize/optimize Tiktok codebase, and make the code/coding become more accessible for Tiktok engineers.","We are looking for talented individuals to join us for an internship in 2025. PhD Internships at TikTok aim to provide students with the opportunity to actively contribute to our products and research, and to the organization's future plans and emerging technologies.","Candidates can apply to a maximum of two positions and will be considered for jobs in the order you apply. The application limit is applicable to TikTok and its affiliates' jobs globally. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis - we encourage you to apply early.","Successful candidates must be able to commit to at least 3 months long internship period.","The main job directions include:","1. Research on LLM Agent methodology, how to build better performance/low cost/stability agents;","2. Explore cutting-edge technologies related to LLM Agent engineering platform(AgentOps), covering areas such as RAG, Reasoning, Planning, Toolkits, Multi-Agents Coordination.","3. Construct a high-performance, cost-effective large-model agent service architecture that ensures high service availability.;","4. Explore the application of frontier LLM agents, like multi-modal video agents, multi-agents coordination on Code AI, etc.","Qualifications","Minimum Qualifications","1. PhD with Computer Science or related fields, with good communication and teamwork skills;","2. Excellent coding ability, data structures, and fundamental algorithm skills, proficient in C/C++ or Python, winners of competitions such as ACM/ICPC, NOI/IOI, Top Coder, Kaggle, etc. are preferred","3. In-depth research and collaboration with researchers from top-tier universities worldwide;","Preferred Qualifications","1. Passion for technology, good communication skills and team spirit","TikTok is committed to creating an inclusive space where employees are valued for their skills, experiences, and unique perspectives. Our platform connects people from across the globe and so does our workplace. At TikTok, our mission is to inspire creativity and bring joy. To achieve 